      "keyInsight": "When entering a new field, beginners often freeze up because they feel underqualified. They assume they must return to school for four years or pretend to be someone they are not. Blake reveals a much faster, smarter way forward called bridging. You do not need to master every single tool in the shed right away. You only need to build the specific skills that bridge where you are today with where you want to be tomorrow. Learning in public, tackling weekend projects, and borrowing skills from your past work helps close the distance rapidly. You do not lack talent; you simply need to link your existing strengths to new demands.",
