      "chapterNumber": 8,
      "headline": "Turn Scarcity Into Your Secret Superpower",
      "keyInsight": "We love to believe that big changes demand giant budgets, flawless tools, and endless free time. That excuse keeps us safely on the couch. But having zero spare resources is actually your greatest creative engine. When a kitchen has twenty fancy ingredients, the cook gets confused. When the pantry holds only garlic, olive oil, and noodles, dinner appears in ten minutes flat. Constraints kill procrastination because they force you to use whatever sits directly on your desk right now. The paradox of getting scrappy is that having less forces you to build smarter, lighter experiments that can never bankrupt you.",
